@{
    Layout = ViewBag.PrintMode == true ? null : "_Layout";
}
@if (ViewBag.PrintMode == true)
{
    <style>
        .sheet {
            padding: 20px;
            font-family: Arial;
        }

        .section {
            margin-bottom: 20px;
        }

        .section-title {
            font-weight: bold;
        }

        .schedule-table {
            width: 100%;
            border-collapse: collapse;
        }

            .schedule-table th, .schedule-table td {
                border: 1px solid #000;
                padding: 5px;
            }
    </style>
}

<div class="spec-section">
    <div class="spec-title">Freight Notes:</div>
    <div class="spec-content">
        <div>• The estimated cost of freight excludes all on‑site permits, equipment, rigging, and manpower needed to unload the described freight.</div>
        <div>• The described freight will be secured to a flatbed trailer or pallet/skid depending on size.</div>
        <div>• Due to global inflation, the estimated cost of freight is subject to change at any time prior to shipment.</div>
        <div>• If unloading is delayed once the shipment has arrived on site, additional rates or fees may apply.</div>
        <div>• Sho‑Me Fabrication, LLC is not responsible for “road grime” and it should be expected when hauled on an open trailer. Consult your SMF representative for packaging solutions. Additional charges may apply.</div>
        <div>• The cost of freight plus a 10% handling charge will be invoiced to the customer once shipment has arrived. Net 30 days.</div>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="spec-section">
    <div class="spec-title">Sho‑Me Fabrication, LLC Terms and Conditions:</div>

    <div class="terms-number">
        <strong>1. Purchase and Sale:</strong>
        The goods described in the attached price quotation (“Goods”) shall be sold in accordance with these terms and conditions and the attached quotation (collectively, the “Sales Order”).
    </div>

    <div class="terms-number">
        <strong>2. Acceptance:</strong>
        Seller shall accept or reject Purchaser’s order within thirty (30) days after receipt.
    </div>

    <div class="terms-number">
        <strong>3. Credit Approval:</strong>
        If Purchaser is permitted to pay all or part of the purchase price after shipment, Seller’s obligations are subject to credit approval.
        If credit is not approved, Purchaser must make all payments on or before shipment as described in the Sales Order.
    </div>

    <div class="terms-number">
        <strong>4. Specifications:</strong>
        If Seller submits drawings or specifications for approval, Purchaser must approve or disapprove within the time specified.
        Failure to respond may result in termination, delay charges, or delivery extensions.
        Seller retains ownership of any designs or specifications created solely by Seller or jointly with Purchaser.
        Purchaser retains ownership of any designs submitted by Purchaser that are not revised by Seller.
    </div>
</div>

